{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"the-frogs-who-sang-too-loud","version":1,"title":"The Frogs Who Sang Too Loud","ageTiers":["7-8","9-10"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"It was the rainy season. Behind Atsu’s house, there was a pond, and in the pond lived a hundred frogs. Every night they sang, ‘Ribbit! Ribbit! Ribbit!’ Atsu could not sleep.","sentences":["It was the rainy season.","Behind Atsu’s house, there was a pond, and in the pond lived a hundred frogs.","Every night they sang, ‘Ribbit!","Ribbit!","Ribbit!’ Atsu could not sleep."],"alt":"A boy lies in bed with a pillow over his head while frogs sing outside.","image":{"hash":"sha256:4f0b7257343ea6e1f857cbee06cd91751a141a680639135b739ef5af61364e13","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:dad664e1e6a51f73596a9c72ec3f559d3127db1bff048fc73d159ae9afe75c1c","durationMs":20000,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2870],[2870,10714],[10714,14541],[14541,16168],[16168,20000]],"words":[[0,191],[191,478],[478,765],[765,1243],[1243,2870],[2870,3444],[3444,3922],[3922,4879],[4879,5357],[5357,5644],[5644,5835],[5835,6696],[6696,6983],[6983,7174],[7174,7461],[7461,7844],[7844,8322],[8322,8513],[8513,9183],[9183,10714],[10714,11192],[11192,11670],[11670,12053],[12053,12914],[12914,14541],[14541,16168],[16168,17795],[17795,18178],[18178,18656],[18656,18943],[18943,20000]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"Atsu put cotton in his ears. It did not help. ‘Those frogs sing too loudly!’ he groaned. ‘Tomorrow, I will chase them all away.’","sentences":["Atsu put cotton in his ears.","It did not help.","‘Those frogs sing too loudly!’ he groaned.","‘Tomorrow, I will chase them all away.’"],"alt":"A boy with cotton in his ears frowns at the window.","image":{"hash":"sha256:0efb95c91870c038c929236f06c9c653870a9077905cbe4f422dc4de3458dfa5","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:204f6d13b11c03a6322be2f5ea59c775dc7eb58c126dec195b12681177b59501","durationMs":13320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2911],[2911,4940],[4940,9704],[9704,13320]],"words":[[0,353],[353,618],[618,1147],[1147,1323],[1323,1588],[1588,2911],[2911,3087],[3087,3352],[3352,3617],[3617,4940],[4940,5381],[5381,5822],[5822,6175],[6175,6440],[6440,7940],[7940,8116],[8116,9704],[9704,10851],[10851,11027],[11027,11380],[11380,11821],[11821,12174],[12174,12439],[12439,13320]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"In the morning, Grandma Korkoi laughed. ‘Do not chase them,’ she said. ‘The boy frogs are singing to call the girl frogs. And a loud pond is a healthy pond.’ ‘Healthy?’ said Atsu.","sentences":["In the morning, Grandma Korkoi laughed.","‘Do not chase them,’ she said.","‘The boy frogs are singing to call the girl frogs.","And a loud pond is a healthy pond.’ ‘Healthy?’ said Atsu."],"alt":"A grandmother smiles at her grandson on the porch.","image":{"hash":"sha256:1840a1032ad0b714aaec5657539e102dbefef1966c9a230b1ad74f228b14f2df","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:b1048af91b6c31856c0e67482b6c0c6aa729ebc14a1110b24694d799c1e214dd","durationMs":18720,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4362],[4362,7725],[7725,12269],[12269,18720]],"words":[[0,182],[182,455],[455,1545],[1545,2181],[2181,2726],[2726,4362],[4362,4544],[4544,4817],[4817,5271],[5271,6089],[6089,6362],[6362,7725],[7725,7998],[7998,8271],[8271,8725],[8725,8998],[8998,9634],[9634,9816],[9816,10179],[10179,10452],[10452,10815],[10815,12269],[12269,12542],[12542,12724],[12724,13087],[13087,13450],[13450,13632],[13632,13814],[13814,14450],[14450,15813],[15813,17449],[17449,17812],[17812,18720]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"‘Frogs eat insects, including mosquitoes,’ said Grandma. ‘And a frog has thin, soft skin that takes in water and air. So it needs clean water to live. When the water is spoiled, frogs go away.’","sentences":["‘Frogs eat insects, including mosquitoes,’ said Grandma.","‘And a frog has thin, soft skin that takes in water and air.","So it needs clean water to live.","When the water is spoiled, frogs go away.’"],"alt":"A frog catches a mosquito with its tongue beside a clean pond.","image":{"hash":"sha256:f83a37da28a160e3fcc25216b82b7c40abaeba0c8b384f6b31d3ece66f4b20dc","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:39d16232fad846d4007d9faf4cf7b1a7a0aa809e75c8c9253d975c339638450a","durationMs":18040,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5752],[5752,11155],[11155,14292],[14292,18040]],"words":[[0,436],[436,697],[697,1743],[1743,2527],[2527,3834],[3834,4183],[4183,5752],[5752,6013],[6013,6187],[6187,6536],[6536,6797],[6797,7581],[7581,7930],[7930,8279],[8279,8628],[8628,9064],[9064,9238],[9238,9674],[9674,9935],[9935,11155],[11155,11329],[11329,11503],[11503,11939],[11939,12375],[12375,12811],[12811,12985],[12985,14292],[14292,14641],[14641,14902],[14902,15338],[15338,15512],[15512,16558],[16558,16994],[16994,17168],[17168,18040]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"A few weeks later, some people threw plastic bags and old bottles near the pond. Mud and rubbish drifted in. The water turned dull and smelly.","sentences":["A few weeks later, some people threw plastic bags and old bottles near the pond.","Mud and rubbish drifted in.","The water turned dull and smelly."],"alt":"Plastic bags and bottles lie at the edge of a muddy pond.","image":{"hash":"sha256:5c38bc303c786dc622dd0723bfcde343b4da58bba011db836fee5e98aab3e615","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:13e73a2212c861c40f35880fc7f8fcde0f1e1e1b86d0e4f919ff4ba897e14b8d","durationMs":18560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,10229],[10229,14396],[14396,18560]],"words":[[0,253],[253,632],[632,1263],[1263,2526],[2526,3031],[3031,3789],[3789,4420],[4420,5304],[5304,5809],[5809,6188],[6188,6567],[6567,7451],[7451,7956],[7956,8335],[8335,10229],[10229,10608],[10608,10987],[10987,11871],[11871,12755],[12755,14396],[14396,14775],[14775,15406],[15406,16164],[16164,16669],[16669,17048],[17048,18560]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"That night, there was no ribbit. No song at all. The house was very quiet. But Atsu still could not sleep. Instead, he heard, ‘Zzzzz!’ Mosquitoes!","sentences":["That night, there was no ribbit.","No song at all.","The house was very quiet.","But Atsu still could not sleep.","Instead, he heard, ‘Zzzzz!’ Mosquitoes!"],"alt":"A boy lies awake in a quiet room, with a mosquito buzzing near his ear.","image":{"hash":"sha256:df53e84158f76749c523e4286abcf992606da50ebef2b11b82f3f0324636fb25","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:1960fe061223e36b4c489ec3e6af08060f47220ee3c88613411218fa84c1f130","durationMs":20840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4593],[4593,7058],[7058,10531],[10531,14564],[14564,20840]],"words":[[0,448],[448,1568],[1568,2128],[2128,2464],[2464,2688],[2688,4593],[4593,4817],[4817,5265],[5265,5489],[5489,7058],[7058,7394],[7394,7954],[7954,8290],[8290,8738],[8738,10531],[10531,10867],[10867,11315],[11315,11875],[11875,12435],[12435,12771],[12771,14564],[14564,15909],[15909,16133],[16133,17253],[17253,19046],[19046,20840]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"‘I miss the frogs,’ said Atsu. ‘So let us help them,’ said Grandma. With gloves and a sack, and with two grown-ups watching, Atsu and his cousins picked up the rubbish from the edge. They did not go into the water.","sentences":["‘I miss the frogs,’ said Atsu.","‘So let us help them,’ said Grandma.","With gloves and a sack, and with two grown-ups watching, Atsu and his cousins picked up the rubbish from the edge.","They did not go into the water."],"alt":"Children in gloves put rubbish into a sack at the edge of a pond while adults watch.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d7c7badc9f4005b62ca71a9a65532207200d5dc79f36f730d9df91284b1a1606","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:562f9e34ecefd5991097285f60ef4078e216b232acfa637a36d3f8ceafc5b051","durationMs":25240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4320],[4320,9094],[9094,21827],[21827,25240]],"words":[[0,227],[227,682],[682,1023],[1023,2160],[2160,2615],[2615,4320],[4320,4547],[4547,4888],[4888,5115],[5115,5570],[5570,6593],[6593,7048],[7048,9094],[9094,9549],[9549,10231],[10231,10572],[10572,10799],[10799,11822],[11822,12163],[12163,12618],[12618,12959],[12959,13869],[13869,15347],[15347,15802],[15802,16143],[16143,16484],[16484,17280],[17280,17962],[17962,18189],[18189,18530],[18530,19326],[19326,19781],[19781,20122],[20122,21827],[21827,22282],[22282,22623],[22623,22964],[22964,23191],[23191,23646],[23646,23987],[23987,25240]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"Months later, the rains came back, and the pond filled with clean water. One night, Atsu heard it again: ‘Ribbit! Ribbit!’ He smiled and slept like a log. The end.","sentences":["Months later, the rains came back, and the pond filled with clean water.","One night, Atsu heard it again: ‘Ribbit!","Ribbit!’ He smiled and slept like a log.","The end."],"alt":"A boy sleeps happily while frogs sing in a clean pond outside.","image":{"hash":"sha256:c499a27c091a2637428b960d23bdf85301b23fde73602854870bf9dafa866315","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:2e696bfe10b660b2dfcce765b100c5c7e9742e5b44bee86787804e809a7621fd","durationMs":20160,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,8109],[8109,13410],[13410,18920],[18920,20160]],"words":[[0,624],[624,1663],[1663,1975],[1975,2495],[2495,2911],[2911,3846],[3846,4158],[4158,4470],[4470,4886],[4886,5510],[5510,5926],[5926,6446],[6446,8109],[8109,8421],[8421,9460],[9460,9876],[9876,10396],[10396,10604],[10604,11643],[11643,13410],[13410,15177],[15177,15385],[15385,16009],[16009,16321],[16321,16841],[16841,17257],[17257,17465],[17465,18920],[18920,19232],[19232,20160]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"frog-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":3,"question":"Why do the boy frogs sing?","options":["To call the girl frogs","To scare Atsu","To ask for food"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"frog-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":4,"question":"Why do frogs need clean water?","options":["Their thin skin takes in water and air","They like bubbles","They dislike mud only"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"frog-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":6,"targetSound":"fr","prompt":"Which words start with the fr sound, like frog?","options":["frog","fish","from","pond"],"correctIndexes":[0,2]},{"id":"frog-p1","type":"prediction","afterPage":7,"prompt":"Atsu and the grown-ups clean the rubbish. What might the frogs do? Tell a friend.","options":["Come back when the water is clean","Never come back"]},{"id":"frog-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the story in order.","items":["Atsu wants the frogs to be quiet.","Grandma tells him about frogs and clean water.","The pond is spoiled and the frogs go quiet.","Atsu helps clean the edge and the frogs return."]},{"id":"frog-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Atsu missed the frogs when they were gone. How do you feel when something you took for granted goes away?","feelingOptions":["Sad","Thoughtful","Thankful","Determined"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"pond","definition":"A small area of still water.","pages":[1,5]},{"word":"mosquitoes","definition":"Small flying insects that bite and can spread illness.","pages":[4,6]},{"word":"healthy","definition":"Well and strong, not ill.","pages":[3]},{"word":"rubbish","definition":"Things that people throw away.","pages":[5,7]}],"assets":{"sha256:4f0b7257343ea6e1f857cbee06cd91751a141a680639135b739ef5af61364e13":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-frogs-who-sang-too-loud/page1-1.webp","bytes":117854,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:dad664e1e6a51f73596a9c72ec3f559d3127db1bff048fc73d159ae9afe75c1c":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/dad664e1e6a5.mp3","bytes":160748,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:0efb95c91870c038c929236f06c9c653870a9077905cbe4f422dc4de3458dfa5":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-frogs-who-sang-too-loud/